# Frozen benchmark artifacts: their BYTES are the identity.
#
# training/eval_set_baseline.json records sha256 over the raw bytes of
# training/eval_set.json, so the file must materialise identically in every
# checkout on every OS.  Git's core.autocrlf=true (the Windows installer's
# system default) otherwise rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout, which changes the
# hash and makes the desync guard in tests/test_run_eval_set.py fail in a fresh
# clone while passing in the worktree the file happened to be written in -- a
# guard whose verdict depends on machine state is not a guard.
#
# The writers already emit LF unconditionally (write_json uses newline="\n"),
# so eol=lf makes the checkout agree with the writer rather than the platform.
training/*.json text eol=lf
